Create, inspect, update, pin, and delete Moment posts.

Usage:
  moment post [flags]
  moment post [command]

Available Commands:
  create        Publish a Moment post
  delete        Delete a Moment post
  get           Get one Moment post
  like          Like one post
  like-status   Read one post like state
  list          List the public Moment timeline
  mentions      Read one post saved mention identities
  pin           Pin one Moment post to the public profile
  reply-context Read one post reply participants
  repost        Repost one Moment to the top of the timeline
  unlike        Remove a like from one post
  unpin         Remove a pinned Moment from the public profile
  unrepost      Remove one Moment repost
  update        Update a Moment post

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for post

Global Flags:
      --as string                     local account username for content operations; not accepted in API mode
      --data-dir string               local Moment data directory (direct mode)
      --json                          write one machine-readable JSON document to stdout
      --log-format string             stderr log format: text or json (default "text")
      --log-level string              stderr log level: error, warn, info, or debug (default "info")
      --no-input                      fail instead of prompting for input
      --reauth-password-file string   private file containing the current password for sensitive API operations
      --timeout duration              maximum command duration (default 30s)
      --token-file string             file containing an account API token
      --url string                    Moment HTTP API base URL (API mode)

Use "moment post [command] --help" for more information about a command.
